 "title": "MC34064, MC33064, NCV33064 undervoltage sensing circuit: 4.6 V reset with open-collector output",
 "source": {
  "document": "MC34064/D",
  "revision": "Rev. 23, February 2026",
  "pages": 14
 },
 "summary": "A three-terminal voltage detector that watches a 5 V logic supply and pulls its reset line low when the supply falls under about 4.6 V. Inside are a bandgap reference trimmed in the package, a comparator with about 20 mV of built-in hysteresis, an NPN open-collector output that sinks more than 10 mA, and a clamp diode from the reset pin back to the input. The output stays defined with the input as low as 1.0 V. MC34064 covers 0 to 70 °C, MC33064 -40 to 85 °C and NCV33064 -40 to 125 °C; MC34064P-5G is the 0 to 70 °C part in TO-92, sold in bags of 2,000.",
 "key_figures": [
