   "id": "low-voltage-reset",
   "title": "Low voltage microprocessor reset",
   "page": 4,
   "description": "The part sits across the supply and drives the processor's reset line. R pulls the open-collector output up to the supply; adding CDLY from the reset line to ground gives a time-delayed reset, set by R and CDLY. For supplies that rise in under 500 ns, R·CDLY should be over 5.0 µs. The internal clamp diode from Reset to Input discharges CDLY.",
